---
description: Next.js implementation guidelines and best practices
globs: apps/web/app/**,next.config.js
alwaysApply: false
---
# Next.js Implementation Guidelines

<rule>
name: atlas_nextjs
description: Standards for implementing proper Next.js applications and patterns
filters:
  - type: file_path
    pattern: "(?:app/|next\\.config\\.js)$"
  - type: content
    pattern: "(?i)next\\.js|nextjs|getserversideprops|getstaticprops|getstaticpaths|app router"

actions:
  - type: suggest
    message: |
      When implementing Next.js code:

      ## App Router
      - Use proper page organization
      - Implement proper layouts
      - Use proper server components
      - Implement proper client components
      - Follow App Router best practices

      ## Data Fetching
      - Use proper server-side fetching
      - Implement proper caching strategies
      - Use proper revalidation
      - Implement proper error handling
      - Follow data fetching best practices

      ## Routing
      - Use proper dynamic routes
      - Implement proper nested routes
      - Use proper parallel routes
      - Implement proper intercepted routes
      - Follow routing best practices

      ## Optimization
      - Use proper image optimization
      - Implement proper font loading
      - Use proper script optimization
      - Implement proper code splitting
      - Follow optimization best practices

      ## Deployment
      - Use proper environment variables
      - Implement proper build configuration
      - Use proper deployment strategies
      - Implement proper monitoring
      - Follow deployment best practices

examples:
  - input: "Creating a new Next.js page"
    output: "Page uses proper data fetching, optimizations, and follows Next.js best practices"

metadata:
  priority: high
  version: 1.0
</rule>